{
 "format": {
  "name": "tessel",
  "version": 1
 },
 "meta": {
  "title": "Invoice email",
  "description": "An email, 600 wide (never a post): the Email frame is the email's card and each child is a section, top to bottom. Restyle it in the brand with set_tokens (color.brand for the button and pill, color.ink, color.paper the card, color.page around it, color.night the footer; font.heading, font.body), put the business's name in Logo and FooterName (or replace Logo with the logo as an image layer named for its alt text) and its own words everywhere. {{field}} words are filled for each person; keep them. A layer named link:<address> links: rename it to the real address. Save it as a template with email_design_save, declaring its fields. An invoice (transactional). Fields: invoice_number, amount_due, due_date, how_to_pay (default \"Reply to this email and we will tell you how to pay.\"), lines (a list: the repeat:lines rows, each {{item}}, {{qty}} and {{amount}}) and note (optional; if:note draws it). Rename the Pay button's layer to the payment link, or delete Action when there is none. Subject \"Invoice {{invoice_number}}\"; preheader \"{{amount_due}} due by {{due_date}}.\""
 },
